# labdash scrontab - install with:  scrontab labdash.scron     (list: scrontab -l)
#
# Slurm's cron. Each firing is a real job on a compute node, so it survives login-node
# reboots, needs nobody logged in, and is the sanctioned way to run recurring work on
# Cannon. A #SCRON block applies to the cron line that follows it.
#
# THIS FILE IS THE ONLY PLACE OUR LAB'S SPECIFICS LIVE. The scripts derive their
# defaults from whoever runs them; everything below that names ydu_lab or a kempner
# path is an override for this deployment. To run labdash for another lab, change:
#   --account=...        the plain Slurm account (four #SCRON blocks + the sbatch line)
#   LABDASH_OUT=...      where the page is written; must be readable by your web publish
#   LABDASH_ROOTS=...    the directories whose children are people's folders (README)
#   $HOME/projects/labdash   if you cloned somewhere else
# then `scrontab labdash.scron`. Our overrides, and why:
#   - LABDASH_OUT points at kempner_ydu_lab's holylabs because ydu_lab's own
#     allocation is at 100% and writes there fail.
#   - LABDASH_ROOTS lists both groups' trees explicitly (kempner_ydu_lab is a second
#     account with its own folders, which the group-derived default would miss).
#
# Never name an interpreter version here. python3.11 was removed from the cluster on
# about 2026-08-22 and every line that hardcoded it began exiting 127 -- silently, for
# days, because a cron job that fails leaves no trace on the page it was supposed to
# update. py.sh resolves whatever exists at run time.
#
# Account must be the plain lab account (ydu_lab), not kempner_ydu_lab: the Kempner
# accounts are restricted to the Kempner partitions and Slurm rejects them on `shared`
# with "Invalid account or account/partition combination specified". Same as gpu_requeue.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dashboard refresh, every 15 minutes. Kept at 15 deliberately: the Pages 503s that
# started at 2026-08-17T15:15Z are GitHub-side (86 consecutive successes before that
# on this identical setup, and failure showed no correlation with the gap between
# pushes -- two pushes 1.7 min apart both deployed fine). Slowing our cadence would
# only paper over someone else's outage, and a failed deploy costs one stale cycle,
# never downtime.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#SCRON --partition=shared
#SCRON --account=ydu_lab
#SCRON --cpus-per-task=1
#SCRON --mem=2G
#SCRON --time=00:10:00
#SCRON --job-name=labdash
#SCRON --output=/dev/null
#SCRON --open-mode=append
*/15 * * * * LABDASH_OUT=/n/holylabs/LABS/kempner_ydu_lab/Lab/labdash LABDASH_PUBLISH=git $HOME/projects/labdash/run.sh

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per-directory scan. This cron entry only SUBMITS the real work: the walk is
# parallel across top-level directories, so it runs as a 32-task array on sapphire
# rather than one long serial job. Sequential holylabs took 87 min; the array's
# wall clock is set by the single slowest directory instead (~13 min there).
# Shards write separate files and labdash unions them by directory name at render.
# Daily is not a compromise here: the per-user quota data it sits beside is itself
# a nightly scan, so polling harder would surface no new information.
# 02:00 keeps it clear of the working day.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#SCRON --partition=shared
#SCRON --account=ydu_lab
#SCRON --cpus-per-task=1
#SCRON --mem=2G
#SCRON --time=00:10:00
#SCRON --job-name=dirscan_submit
#SCRON --output=/dev/null
0 2 * * * cd $HOME/projects/labdash && LABDASH_OUT=/n/holylabs/LABS/kempner_ydu_lab/Lab/labdash LABDASH_ROOTS="/n/holylabs/LABS/ydu_lab/Lab /n/holylabs/LABS/ydu_lab/Everyone /n/holylabs/LABS/kempner_ydu_lab/Lab /n/holylabs/LABS/kempner_ydu_lab/Everyone /n/lab_storage/ydu_lab /n/netscratch/ydu_lab/Lab /n/netscratch/ydu_lab/Everyone" sbatch --parsable --account=ydu_lab dirscan_array.sbatch

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Storage alert to Slack. Once a day, in the morning - NOT on the 15-minute
# refresh: even with the crossing/repeat rules, an alerter that can speak at 3am
# is one people mute. Storage only; the non-preemptible-partition nudge is meant
# to go out by email instead, which is waiting on the roster addresses.
#
# All three locations are discovered automatically, including /n/lab_storage/<lab>
# -- Isilon only reveals a fileset's 100 TiB limit when df is asked about the
# directory itself, not the mount point.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#SCRON --partition=shared
#SCRON --account=ydu_lab
#SCRON --cpus-per-task=1
#SCRON --mem=2G
#SCRON --time=00:10:00
#SCRON --job-name=labdash_alert
#SCRON --output=/dev/null
0 9 * * * LABDASH_OUT=/n/holylabs/LABS/kempner_ydu_lab/Lab/labdash $HOME/projects/labdash/py.sh $HOME/projects/labdash/notify.py --storage-only --threshold 90

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Roster refresh - picks up new lab members, keeps emails already typed in.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#SCRON --partition=shared
#SCRON --account=ydu_lab
#SCRON --cpus-per-task=1
#SCRON --mem=2G
#SCRON --time=00:15:00
#SCRON --job-name=roster
#SCRON --output=/dev/null
30 2 * * * LABDASH_GROUPS="ydu_lab kempner_ydu_lab" $HOME/projects/labdash/py.sh $HOME/projects/labdash/roster.py --out /n/holylabs/LABS/kempner_ydu_lab/Lab/labdash
